{"archetypes":[{"name":"script-ground-truth","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan documents emit_finding/emit_oos field sets and lib-design-round-artifacts allowlist items without verifying those claims against the landed scripts — a mismatch makes all downstream doc changes wrong.","prompt_body":"Verify that each planned documentation change is grounded in actual script behavior rather than assumed behavior. Read skills/design/scripts/plan-review-loop.sh to confirm the emit_finding and emit_oos field sets match what the plan prescribes for the FINDING_N and OOS_N templates in plan-review.md. Read scripts/lib-design-round-artifacts.sh to confirm every per-round artifact path the plan proposes to enumerate in docs/run-logs.md is actually allowlisted there. Read skills/design/scripts/revise-plan-with-waterfall.sh to confirm the canonical-path constraint, snapshot lifecycle, and output-directory confinement described in the planned SECURITY.md paragraph are accurate. Any discrepancy between planned prose and current script code is a plan defect that requires a corrected description or an explicit note that the behavior diverges from what was inspected. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cross-doc-integrity","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Nine files are modified; each adds cross-references or duplicates semantics (severity mapping, env-var defaults, OOS accumulation contract) that must be identical across docs — silent contradictions mislead operators.","prompt_body":"Check that every planned cross-reference points to a section that will exist after the plan is applied — e.g., that the approval-gates.md State invariants carve-out matches the oos-accepted-design.md accumulation prose in plan-review.md, and that env-var defaults documented in flags.md and docs/configuration-and-permissions.md are identical. Verify that the severity mapping (important→High, latent→Medium, nit→Low) appears with the same terms and casing everywhere the plan places it. Confirm that the docs/installation-and-setup.md cross-reference to docs/configuration-and-permissions.md names the correct section header that will exist after the plan is applied. Flag any case where two planned prose blocks describe the same behavior but use inconsistent terminology, default values, or boundary conditions that would contradict each other. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-pin-adequacy","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The two new structure-test assertions are the only CI safety net against doc drift; if their literal substrings are too broad or target wrong files they will pass even after a regression.","prompt_body":"Evaluate whether each planned structure-test assertion in scripts/test-design-structure.sh is narrow enough to catch the failure modes identified in the plan's Failure modes section. Check that the FINDING_N template assertion matches every required field name exactly as the plan spells them and that the severity-precedence assertion checks for all three mapping terms in the correct file (approval-gates.md, not plan-review.md). Verify that the assertion strings would fail if the relevant prose were removed or the field names renamed, and that the proposed check identifiers follow the existing numbering convention already present in the file. Confirm that the agent-lint.toml registration rows for scripts/test-revise-plan-with-waterfall.sh match the category and column format of the sibling rows the plan cites. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
